cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MaplePy or Hopper, please cite the paper below. A versioned release with its own DOI will follow."
title: "MaplePy: MAPLE from crystallographic information files, with a test of Hoppe's additivity theorem"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Reeves-McLaren
    given-names: Nik
    affiliation: University of Sheffield
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1061-1230"
abstract: >-
  MaplePy computes per-site and total MAPLE (Madelung Part of Lattice
  Energy) values from CIF files with the Ewald summation in pymatgen.
  Hopper decomposes ternary oxides into their binary oxides, computes the
  residual of Hoppe's additivity theorem against a 112-entry binary oxide
  reference table, and classifies each structure. This repository holds
  the unversioned notebooks uploaded on 21st May 2026.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SuperBladesman/MaplePy"
keywords:
  - crystallography
  - MAPLE
  - Madelung energy
  - lattice energy
  - additivity theorem
  - crystal structure validation
  - ICSD
  - CIF
